h in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nepal on 5 July 2026.\"},{\"question\":\"Which processor does the POCO M8s use?\",\"answer\":\"It uses the Qualcomm Snapdragon 6s Gen 3 (6 nm).\"},{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8s battery like?\",\"answer\":\"Si-C 7000 mAh, non-removable; 33W Charging; 18W Reverse Wired Charging.\"}]','[{\"label\":\"GadgetByte Nepal \\u2013 POCO M8s\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.gadgetbytenepal.com\\/product\\/poco-m8s\\/\",\"accessed\":\"2026-11-23\"}]',NULL,NULL,0,'2026-07-04 18:15:00','2026-07-04 18:15:00'),(954,3,2,'POCO M8 Pro','poco-m8-pro',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,58999.00,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-07-05','available',NULL,0,0,'<p>The POCO M8 Pro costs <strong>Rs 58,999</strong> in Nepal for the 8GB/256GB model. It launched in Nepal on 5 July 2026. This is the sweet spot: enough for an AMOLED screen and fast charging without paying for flagship cameras.</p>\n<p>It has a 6.83 inches AMOLED, 120Hz, 1800 nits (HBM), 3200 nits (Peak) screen and runs on the Qualcomm Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 (4nm). Its Si-C 6500 mAh, non-removable battery should last a full day for most people. Charging: 100W HyperCharge, 22.5W Reverse Wired Charging. Cameras: Primary: 50MP, f/1.6, 24 mm, OIS, PDAF, 1/1.55\" Light Fusion 800 sensor + Ultrawide: 8MP, f/2.2, 15 mm, 120° FOV, 1/4.0\"OV08D sensor. It is rated IP66/IP68/IP69/IP69K for dust and water. Software support: 4 years of OS updates; 6 years of security updates.</p>\n<p>Around the same budget, also look at the <a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G</a> (Rs 57,999) and the <a href=\"/products/poco-x7-pro\">Poco X7 Pro</a> (Rs 59,999). You can <a href=\"/compare?category=mobile&g1=poco-m8-pro&g2=redmi-note-17-pro-5g\">compare the POCO M8 Pro with the Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G</a> side by side.</p>','[{\"question\":\"What is the POCO M8 Pro price in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"The POCO M8 Pro costs Rs 58,999 in Nepal.\"},{\"question\":\"When did the POCO M8 Pro launch in Nepal?\",\"answer\":\"It launched in Nep