intel-core-ultra-7-256v\">Lenovo ThinkPad E16 Gen 3 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 256V)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,38,450</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-loq-2024-intel-i5-12450hx-rtx-4050\">Lenovo LOQ 15 15IAX9 2024 (Intel Core i5-12450HX)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,45,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-5-15ahp10\">Lenovo Legion 5 (2025)</a></td><td>Ryzen 7 260 · RTX 5060, 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-thinkpad-p14s-gen-6-2025-ryzen-ai-7-pro-350\">Lenovo ThinkPad P14s Gen 6 2025 (Ryzen AI 7 PRO 350)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-thinkpad-x9-14-gen-1-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-258v\">Lenovo ThinkPad X9-14 Gen 1 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 258V)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,78,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-5-15iax10-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-255hx-rtx-5060\">Lenovo Legion 5 15IAX10 2025</a></td><td>Intel Core Ultra 7 255HX, RTX 5060, 16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,84,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX, RTX 5070, 32GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 5,39,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-thinkpad-l16-gen-2-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-255h\">Lenovo ThinkPad L16 Gen 2 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 255H)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,89,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-ideapad-pro-5-16iah10-2025\">Lenovo IdeaPad Pro 5 16IAH10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 285H)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,89,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-thinkpad-x13-gen-6-2025\">Lenovo ThinkPad X13 Gen 6 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 255H)</a></td><td>32GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 3,24,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-loq-15-15irx10-intel-i7-13650hx-rtx-5050\">Lenovo LOQ 15 15IRX10 2025 (Intel Core i7-13650HX)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 3,31,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-loq-15-15ahp11-2026-ryzen-7-250-rtx-5060\">Lenovo LOQ 15 15AHP11 2026 (Ryzen 7 250)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 3,45,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-7i-16iax10-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-275hx-rtx-5060\">Lenovo Legion 7i 16IAX10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 3,49,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-yoga-9-2-in-1-gen-10-2025\">Lenovo Yoga 9 2-in-1 Gen 10 (2025)</a></td><td>Intel Core Ultra 7 258V, 32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 3,60,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-yoga-9-14ill10-2025-core-ultra-7-258v\">Lenovo Yoga 9 Gen 5 14ILL10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 258V)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 3,69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-5a-g11-15agp11-2026-amd-ryzen-ai-9-465-rtx-5060\">Lenovo Legion 5a G11 15AGP11 2026 (AMD Ryzen AI 9 465)</a></td><td>32GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 4,76,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-pro-5i-16iax10-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-275hx-rtx-5060\">Lenovo Legion Pro 5i 16IAX10 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 4,95,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-pro-5-16afr10-2025-ryzen-9-9955hx-rtx-5070\">Lenovo Legion Pro 5 16AFR10 2025 (Ryzen 9 9955HX)</a></td><td>32GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 5,23,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-pro-7i-2025\">Lenovo Legion Pro 7i (2025)</a></td><td>RTX 5080, 32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 7,73,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>RTX 5090, 32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 9,93,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-pro-7i-16iax10h-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-275hx-rtx-5090\">Lenovo Legion Pro 7i 16IAX10H 2025</a></td><td>Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX, RTX 5080, 32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 7,73,900</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX, RTX 5090, 32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 9,93,900</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Where we\'d start</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Students on a budget:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/lenovo-ideapad-slim-3-15irh10-2025-intel-core-i5-13420h\">IdeaPad Slim 3 15IRH10</a> uses a faster H-series Core i5. Pick a 16GB configuration.</li>\n<li><strong>Business:</strong> ThinkPads come with 3-year warranties through ONIN Infosys. The <a href=\"/products/lenovo-thinkpad-e14-gen-7-core-ultra-5-225u\">ThinkPad E14 Gen 7</a> is a solid start.</li>\n<li><strong>Gaming value:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/lenovo-loq-15-2025\">LOQ 15 with RTX 5050</a> at 100W is one of the best-value gaming laptops here.</li>\n<li><strong>High-end gaming:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/lenovo-legion-pro-7i-2025\">Legion Pro 7i</a> with an RTX 5080 has an OLED screen and top-tier cooling.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Avoid the cheapest IdeaPads with Intel N100 chips or Athlon processors unless the laptop is for very light use. More picks are in our <a href=\"/guides/best-laptops-under-150000-nepal\">laptops under Rs 1,50,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/lenovo-legion-pro-7i-2025.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(61,20,'MSI Laptop Price in Nepal (November 2026)','msi-laptop-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>MSI is best known for gaming laptops, but its Nepal range also includes the Modern series of office laptops and the Prestige and Summit lines for creators and business users. Prices run from Rs 92,000 to Rs 6,25,000 for the <a href=\"/products/msi-vector-16-hx-ai-2025\">Vector 16 HX AI</a>.</p>\n<h2>MSI laptops price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-modern-14-2022-i5-1235u\">MSI Modern 14 C12M 2022 (12th Gen i5-1235U)</a></td><td>8GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 92,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-modern-14-2024-intel-core-7-150u\">MSI Modern 14 F1MG 2024</a></td><td>Intel Core 5 120U, 8GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 93,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Intel Core 7 150U, 16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 1,25,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-modern-15-2023-i5-1335u\">MSI Modern 15 B13M 2023</a></td><td>Intel Core i5-1335U, 8GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,05,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Intel Core i7-1355U, 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,27,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-modern-15-h-2023-i5-13420h\">MSI Modern 15 H B13M 2023</a></td><td>Intel Core i5-13420H, 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,13,050</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Intel Core i7-13700H, 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,30,150</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-summit-e13-ai-evo-a1mtg-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-155h\">MSI Summit E13 AI Evo A1MTG 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 7 155H)</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 1,79,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-summit-e16-flip-evo-2023-i7-1360p-165hz\">MSI Summit E16 Flip Evo A11UCT 2023 (Intel Core i7-1360P)</a></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 1,95,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-katana-15-2023-i7-13620h-rtx-4060\">MSI Katana 15 B13VEK 2023 (Intel Core i7-13620H)</a></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,09,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-pulse-15-b13v-i7-13700h-rtx-4060-360hz\">MSI Pulse 15 B13V 2023 (Intel Core i7-13700H)</a></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,23,250</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-prestige-16-studio-2023-i7-13700h-rtx-4050\">MSI Prestige 16 Studio A13V 2023 (Intel Core i7-13700H)</a></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,35,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-stealth-16-ai-studio-intel-core-ultra-7-155h-rtx-4060\">MSI Stealth 16 AI Studio A1VFG 2024 (Intel Core Ultra 7 155H)</a></td><td>32GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,60,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-vector-gp68-hx-2023-i9-13980hx-rtx-4070\">MSI Vector GP68 HX 13VG 2023 (Intel Core i9-13980HX)</a></td><td>32GB/2TB</td><td>Rs 3,47,700</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-vector-16-hx-ai-a2xwjg-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-275hx-rtx-5090\">MSI Vector 16 HX AI A2XWJG 2025 (Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX)</a></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 6,10,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/msi-vector-16-hx-ai-2025\">MSI Vector 16 HX AI (2025)</a></td><td>Core Ultra 7 275HX · RTX 5090, 16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 6,25,000</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What to look at</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Office work:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/msi-modern-14-2024-intel-core-7-150u\">Modern 14 F1MG</a> is good value in its Core 7 150U, 16GB, 1TB configuration. MSI\'s Modern laptops are simple but well built.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry gaming:</strong> the Katana and Cyborg lines. Check the GPU wattage, because some newer Cyborg models limit the RTX 5050 to 45W.</li>\n<li><strong>For creators:</strong> the Prestige 16 Studio and Stealth 16 AI Studio combine good screens with dedicated GPUs in slimmer bodies.</li>\n<li><strong>High end:</strong> the Vector 16 HX AI with an RTX 5090 at 175W is among the most affordable RTX 5090 laptops in Nepal.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Some MSI listings here are older 2022–2023 models. They\'re fine if discounted, but compare them with newer laptops at the same price in our <a href=\"/guides/best-laptops-under-200000-nepal\">laptops under Rs 2,00,000</a> guide.</p>',NULL,1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(62,20,'Motorola Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','motorola-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Motorola phones are popular with people who want clean, close-to-stock Android without extra apps, plus solid batteries. The Nepal range runs from the Rs 30,699 <a href=\"/products/motorola-moto-g35-5g\">Moto G35 5G</a> to the Rs 79,999 <a href=\"/products/motorola-edge-70-fusion\">Edge 70 Fusion</a>.</p>\n<h2>Motorola phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/motorola-moto-g35-5g\">Motorola Moto G35 5G</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 30,699</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/moto-g06-power\">Motorola Moto G06 Power</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 31,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/moto-g57-power\">Motorola Moto G57 Power</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 37,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/moto-g96\">Motorola Moto G96 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/motorola-edge-50-fusion\">Motorola Edge 50 Fusion</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 46,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/motorola-edge-70-fusion\">Motorola Edge 70 Fusion</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 79,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 89,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Moto?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best value:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/moto-g96\">Moto G96 5G</a> (Rs 44,999) has a 120Hz AMOLED screen, OIS on the main camera and IP68 water resistance, which is rare at this price.</li>\n<li><strong>Battery first:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/moto-g57-power\">Moto G57 Power</a> (Rs 37,499) has a big battery and the fastest chip in its group. Note that it ships without a charger.</li>\n<li><strong>The best Motorola here:</strong> the Edge 70 Fusion, with a 7,000mAh battery, a 120Hz AMOLED and a Snapdragon 7s Gen 4.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The G06 Power and G35 are basic phones. Look at Samsung\'s and Xiaomi\'s options at the same price in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-40000-nepal\">phones under Rs 40,000</a> guide before you decide.</p>','gadgets/2026/motorola-edge-70-fusion.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(63,20,'Noise Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','noise-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Noise is an Indian brand that\'s popular in Nepal for cheap, stylish earbuds. Its current range here is small and tightly priced, from the Rs 2,699 <a href=\"/products/noise-buds-trance-2\">Buds Trance 2</a> to the Rs 3,999 <a href=\"/products/noise-aura-buds\">Aura Buds</a>.</p>\n<h2>Noise earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/noise-buds-trance-2\">Noise Buds Trance 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,699</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/noise-buds-n1\">Noise Buds N1</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,799</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/noise-mvp-102-gaming\">Noise MVP 102 Gaming</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,399</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/noise-aura-buds\">Noise Aura Buds</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What to expect</h2>\n<p>All four models are everyday earbuds for calls, YouTube and music on the go. The <strong>Aura Buds</strong> have the most eye-catching design, the <a href=\"/products/noise-buds-n1\">Buds N1</a> are a plain, reliable choice, and the <strong>MVP 102 Gaming</strong> buds have a low-latency mode, so mobile game sound doesn\'t lag behind the action.</p>\n<p>The gap to better brands is small at this price. Before you buy, compare them with the <a href=\"/products/kick-phantom-buds-x-pro\">Kick Phantom Buds X Pro</a> (Rs 2,599), which adds noise cancellation, and with the other picks in our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 5,000</a> guide. Noise cancellation and a good mic matter more day to day than the look of the case.</p>','gadgets/2026/noise-aura-buds.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(64,20,'Nothing Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','nothing-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Nothing\'s earbuds in Nepal are sold under its cheaper <strong>CMF</strong> sub-brand, and they\'re some of the best value around. You get modern features like noise cancellation and multipoint without paying flagship prices. The range runs from Rs 5,999 for the <a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2a\">CMF Buds 2a</a> to Rs 14,999 for the <a href=\"/products/cmf-clip-pro\">CMF Clip Pro</a>.</p>\n<h2>Nothing earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2a\">CMF Buds 2a</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2\">CMF Buds 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 7,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2-plus\">CMF Buds 2 Plus</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 8,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-pro-2\">CMF Buds Pro 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 9,599</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/cmf-clip-pro\">CMF Clip Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 14,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best all-rounder:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2-plus\">CMF Buds 2 Plus</a> (Rs 8,999) has noise cancellation, LDAC for higher-quality audio on Android, and multipoint, so it switches between your phone and laptop.</li>\n<li><strong>On a tighter budget:</strong> the Buds 2a and <a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2\">Buds 2</a> cover the basics well, with ANC included.</li>\n<li><strong>Open-ear comfort:</strong> the Clip Pro clips onto your ear instead of sealing it, so you can still hear traffic and conversations. It\'s good for walking and long wear, but weaker for blocking noise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CMF earbuds work with any phone through the Nothing X app. For other brands at similar prices, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-10000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 10,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/cmf-buds-2-plus.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(65,20,'Nothing Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','nothing-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Nothing\'s phones are easy to spot thanks to their see-through backs and Glyph lights, but there\'s more to them than looks. The software is clean and fast, and the prices are sensible. The Nepal range runs from Rs 54,999 for the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3a-lite\">Phone 3a Lite</a> to Rs 1,09,999 for the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3\">Phone (3)</a> and <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4a-pro\">Phone 4a Pro</a>.</p>\n<h2>Nothing phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3a-lite\">Nothing Phone 3a Lite</a></td><td>8/128GB</td><td>Rs 54,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4b\">Nothing Phone 4b</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-3\">Nothing Phone (3)</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,09,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4a-pro\">Nothing Phone 4a Pro</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,09,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Nothing phone?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The value pick:</strong> the Phone 3a Lite has a 120Hz AMOLED screen and a Dimensity 7300 Pro, a smooth everyday phone with Nothing\'s design.</li>\n<li><strong>A camera with zoom:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4a\">Phone 4a</a> is one of the cheapest phones in Nepal with a periscope zoom. Compare it in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-in-nepal-by-budget\">phones by budget</a> guide.</li>\n<li><strong>Flagship speed:</strong> the Phone (3), with a Snapdragon 8s Gen 4, IP68 and 16GB/512GB, is the most powerful Nothing phone here.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Nothing promises several years of updates on these models, which is reassuring at this price. The <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4b\">Phone 4b</a> sits between the Lite and the 4a if you want something in the middle.</p>','gadgets/2026/nothing-phone-3.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(66,20,'OPPO Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','oppo-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>OPPO has a big presence in Nepal, with phones from the Rs 22,999 <a href=\"/products/oppo-a5\">A5</a> to the Rs 2,49,999 <a href=\"/products/oppo-find-n5\">Find N5</a> foldable. The <strong>A series</strong> covers budget phones, the <strong>Reno</strong> series is mid-range with a focus on portrait cameras, and <strong>Find</strong> is the flagship range.</p>\n<h2>OPPO phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a5\">OPPO A5</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 22,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 24,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 27,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6c\">OPPO A6c</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 24,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 30,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6x\">OPPO A6x</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 27,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 32,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 34,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6k-4g\">OPPO A6k 4G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 38,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 43,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6\">OPPO A6</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 40,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 46,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6-pro-4g\">OPPO A6 Pro 4G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 51,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6s-pro\">OPPO A6s Pro</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 56,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-15-f\">OPPO Reno 15F</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 63,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-15-5g\">OPPO Reno 15</a></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 89,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-16f-5g\">OPPO Reno 16F</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 89,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-16-5g\">OPPO Reno 16</a></td><td>12GB - 256GB - Phone Only</td><td>Rs 1,09,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB - 256GB - With OPPO Bubble</td><td>Rs 1,19,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-find-x9-pro\">OPPO Find X9 Pro</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,25,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,35,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,42,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 1,58,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oppo-find-n5\">Oppo Find N5</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,49,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Worth a look</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A tough phone on a budget:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/oppo-a6\">OPPO A6</a> (from Rs 40,999) has a 7,000mAh battery and IP68 water resistance, a rare combination at this price.</li>\n<li><strong>Mid-range:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-16-5g\">Reno 16</a> and <a href=\"/products/oppo-reno-16f-5g\">Reno 16F</a> are good for people who take a lot of portrait and social photos. The 16F\'s 7,000mAh battery is a highlight.</li>\n<li><strong>Flagship:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/oppo-find-x9-pro\">Find X9 Pro</a> (Rs 1,25,999) pairs a Dimensity 9500 with a 7,500mAh battery, and costs less than most rival flagships.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cheapest A-series models (A6c, A6x) come with as little as 4GB/64GB, so aim for 128GB of storage. The new <a href=\"/news/oppo-reno-17-launched-8000mah-battery\">Reno 17</a> has launched in China and is expected here later.</p>','gadgets/2026/oppo-find-x9-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(67,20,'OnePlus Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','oneplus-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>OnePlus phones in Nepal offer a lot of speed for the money, with big batteries and fast charging. The range runs from the Rs 59,999 <a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-ce-5\">Nord CE5</a> to the Rs 1,89,999 <a href=\"/products/oneplus-15\">OnePlus 15</a>.</p>\n<h2>OnePlus phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-ce-5\">OnePlus Nord CE5</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-5\">OnePlus Nord 5</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 73,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 79,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-ce-6\">OnePlus Nord CE6</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 74,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-6\">OnePlus Nord 6</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 89,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-15r\">OnePlus 15R</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 98,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,06,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-13s\">OnePlus 13s</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,19,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/oneplus-15\">OnePlus 15</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,89,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which OnePlus?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best value in the range:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/oneplus-15r\">OnePlus 15R</a> (from Rs 98,499) has flagship-level performance for under a lakh. For most people, it\'s the one to buy.</li>\n<li><strong>Budget OnePlus:</strong> the Nord CE5 has a 7,100mAh battery and a Dimensity 8350 Apex, which is plenty fast for under Rs 60,000. The <a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-ce-6\">Nord CE6</a> is the newer model.</li>\n<li><strong>The flagship:</strong> the OnePlus 15, with a Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5 and a 7,300mAh battery, rivals Samsung\'s best on speed and battery life.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/oneplus-13s\">OnePlus 13s</a> is a compact phone with 16GB/512GB, a good fit if you prefer a smaller handset.</p>','gadgets/2026/oneplus-15.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(68,20,'Realme Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','realme-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Realme\'s earbuds offer a lot of features for little money. The range here runs from the Rs 2,499 <a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t100\">Buds T100</a> to the Rs 8,499 <a href=\"/products/realme-buds-air-8\">Buds Air 8</a>.</p>\n<h2>Realme earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t100\">Realme Buds T100</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200x\">Realme Buds T200x</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200\">Realme Buds T200</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t500-pro\">Realme Buds T500 Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-air-8\">Realme Buds Air 8</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 8,499</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best value:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200\">Buds T200</a> (Rs 4,499) has noise cancellation, LDAC for better audio on Android, and multipoint. That\'s a lot for under Rs 5,000.</li>\n<li><strong>Cheapest with good basics:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200x\">Buds T200x</a> (Rs 2,999) includes ANC and a long battery life.</li>\n<li><strong>Best Realme earbuds:</strong> the Buds Air 8, with stronger noise cancellation and better sound tuning.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The T100 is a simple pair for calls and music. If you\'re buying under Rs 3,000, also compare the <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-5a\">Redmi Buds 5A</a> in our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-3000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 3,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/realme-buds-t200.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(69,20,'Realme Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','realme-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Realme sells phones at almost every price in Nepal, from the Rs 15,999 <a href=\"/products/realme-note-60x\">Note 60x</a> to the Rs 1,49,999 <a href=\"/products/realme-gt-8-pro\">GT 8 Pro</a>. The <strong>Note</strong> and <strong>C</strong> series are budget phones, <strong>P</strong> is the value range, and <strong>GT</strong> is the performance range.</p>\n<h2>Realme phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-note-60x\">Realme Note 60x</a></td><td>3GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 15,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 16,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 21,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-note-70\">Realme Note 70</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 16,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 20,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 23,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-note-80\">Realme Note 80</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 21,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c71\">Realme C71</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 25,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c100i\">Realme C100i</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 28,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p4-lite-4g\">Realme P4 Lite 4G</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 31,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p4x-4g\">Realme P4x 4G</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c100x\">Realme C100x</a></td><td>4GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 35,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c85-pro\">Realme C85 Pro</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 36,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c85-5g\">Realme C85 5G</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-c85\">Realme C85</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p3\">Realme P3</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p4-4g\">Realme P4 4G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 45,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-14-5g\">Realme 14 5G</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 49,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-16-5g\">Realme 16</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p3-ultra\">Realme P3 Ultra</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 65,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-15-pro\">Realme 15 Pro</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 66,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 71,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-p4-power\">Realme P4 Power</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 76,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/realme-gt-8-pro\">Realme GT 8 Pro</a></td><td>Standard (Wind Moves White), 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,49,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Aston Martin Edition, 16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,59,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Highlights from the range</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tough and affordable:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/realme-c85-5g\">Realme C85 5G</a> (from Rs 39,999) has a 7,000mAh battery and IP68. The <a href=\"/products/realme-c85-pro\">C85 Pro</a> adds an AMOLED screen and even higher water ratings.</li>\n<li><strong>Battery champion:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/realme-p4-power\">Realme P4 Power</a> has a 10,001mAh battery. It\'s one of the longest-lasting phones on sale.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance:</strong> the GT 8 Pro, with a Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen 5 and 7,000mAh, competes with flagships costing much more.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Realme\'s cheapest Note models have small storage. Pick at least 128GB, as covered in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-25000-nepal\">phones under Rs 25,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/realme-gt-8-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(70,20,'Samsung Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','samsung-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Samsung\'s Galaxy Buds work with any phone, but they make the most sense with a Galaxy phone. Switching between devices, Galaxy AI interpretation and the best audio quality all depend on Samsung\'s own software. Prices in Nepal run from Rs 7,999 for the <a href=\"/products/galaxy-buds-core\">Galaxy Buds Core</a> to Rs 35,799 for the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-buds4-pro\">Galaxy Buds 4 Pro</a>.</p>\n<h2>Samsung earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/galaxy-buds-core\">Galaxy Buds Core</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 7,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-buds3-fe\">Samsung Galaxy Buds 3 FE</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 19,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sasmung-galaxy-buds3\">Samsung Galaxy Buds3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 22,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-buds4\">Samsung Galaxy Buds 4</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 26,099</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-buds3-pro\">Samsung Galaxy Buds 3 Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 31,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-buds4-pro\">Samsung Galaxy Buds 4 Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 35,799</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Galaxy Buds?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>On a budget:</strong> the Buds Core. It has noise cancellation, a secure fit, and easy pairing with Galaxy phones.</li>\n<li><strong>The middle of the range:</strong> the Buds 3 FE and <a href=\"/products/sasmung-galaxy-buds3\">Buds 3</a>. The Buds 3 has an open, stem design that some people find more comfortable than a sealed fit.</li>\n<li><strong>The best:</strong> the Buds 4 Pro has Samsung\'s strongest noise cancellation and its best sound. Pair it with a recent Galaxy S phone.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you don\'t use a Samsung phone, you\'ll get similar features for less from Soundcore or CMF. See our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-20000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 20,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/samsung-galaxy-buds4-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(71,20,'Samsung Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','samsung-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Samsung has the broadest phone range in Nepal and the biggest service network, which is a big reason many people stick with Galaxy phones. Prices run from Rs 25,499 for the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a07\">Galaxy A07</a> to Rs 2,99,999 for the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-fold-8-ultra\">Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra</a>. The <strong>A and M</strong> series are budget and mid-range, <strong>S</strong> is the flagship range, and <strong>Z</strong> covers the foldables.</p>\n<h2>Samsung phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a07\">Samsung Galaxy A07</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 25,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 29,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 33,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a07s\">Samsung Galaxy A07s</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 30,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a08\">Samsung Galaxy A08</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 34,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 40,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 47,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-m36-5g\">Samsung Galaxy M36 5G</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 41,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 47,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-m17-5g\">Samsung Galaxy M17 5G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 43,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a17-5g\">Samsung Galaxy A17 5G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 48,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 56,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a27-5g\">Samsung Galaxy A27 5G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 55,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a37-5g\">Samsung Galaxy A37 5G</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 74,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 86,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 96,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a57-5g\">Samsung Galaxy A57 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 96,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,07,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-fe\">Samsung Galaxy S26 FE</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,24,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-flip7-fe\">Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 7 FE</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,35,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26\">Samsung Galaxy S26</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-flip-7\">Samsung Galaxy Z Flip7</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,54,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s25-ultra\">Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,84,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-flip8\">Samsung Galaxy Z Flip 8</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,94,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-ultra\">Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 2,24,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 2,59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>16GB/1TB</td><td>Rs 2,93,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-fold-7\">Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 7</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 2,59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-fold8\">Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 2,74,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-z-fold-8-ultra\">Samsung Galaxy Z Fold 8 Ultra</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 2,99,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 3,39,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks by budget</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Under Rs 50,000:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a17-5g\">Galaxy A17 5G</a> (from Rs 44,999) has a Super AMOLED screen and OIS camera, plus Samsung\'s long software support. The <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-m36-5g\">Galaxy M36 5G</a> (Rs 41,999) is a strong alternative.</li>\n<li><strong>Mid-range:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a37-5g\">Galaxy A37 5G</a> adds IP68 and a better camera.</li>\n<li><strong>Best value flagship:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s25-ultra\">Galaxy S25 Ultra</a> (Rs 1,84,999) is now Rs 40,000 cheaper than the S26 Ultra. <a href=\"/news/samsung-galaxy-s25-ultra-leak-roundup-snapdragon-8-elite-nepal\">Our comparison</a> explains what you give up.</li>\n<li><strong>The newest:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-ultra\">Galaxy S26 Ultra</a> and <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-fe\">S26 FE</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cheapest A0x models are basic, and 4GB/64GB fills up quickly. Samsung Nepal often runs EMI and data offers, covered in <a href=\"/news/samsung-ncell-partnership-galaxy-offers-nepal\">our Samsung–Ncell report</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/samsung-galaxy-s25-ultra.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(72,20,'Samsung Smartwatch Price in Nepal (November 2026)','samsung-smartwatch-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Galaxy Watches are the natural choice for Samsung phone owners. They handle notifications, replies, payments and health tracking in a way most other watches can\'t match on Android. The range in Nepal runs from the Rs 7,999 <a href=\"/products/galaxy-fit-3\">Galaxy Fit 3</a> band to the Rs 1,23,499 <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-ultra-2\">Galaxy Watch Ultra 2</a>.</p>\n<h2>Samsung smartwatches price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/galaxy-fit-3\">Samsung Galaxy Fit 3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 7,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-fe\">Samsung Galaxy Watch FE</a></td><td>40mm</td><td>Rs 21,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-7\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 7</a></td><td>40mm (Wi-Fi only)</td><td>Rs 28,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>44mm (Wi-Fi only)</td><td>Rs 31,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-6\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 6</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-8\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 8</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 61,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-6-classic\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 6 Classic</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch9\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 9</a></td><td>40mm</td><td>Rs 66,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>44mm</td><td>Rs 71,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch8-classic\">Samsung Galaxy Watch 8 Classic</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 82,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-ultra\">Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra</a></td><td>47mm</td><td>Rs 1,15,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-ultra-2\">Samsung Galaxy Watch Ultra 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 1,23,499</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Galaxy watch?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fitness tracking only:</strong> the Galaxy Fit 3. It\'s a simple band with long battery life.</li>\n<li><strong>Best value smartwatch:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-fe\">Galaxy Watch FE</a> (Rs 21,999) gives you the full Wear OS experience, GPS and an AMOLED screen at the lowest price.</li>\n<li><strong>The newest:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-8\">Galaxy Watch 8</a> and Watch 9 add better health sensors and brighter screens.</li>\n<li><strong>Outdoors and trekking:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-watch-ultra\">Watch Ultra</a> and Ultra 2 have titanium cases and the longest battery life in the range.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Battery life on Galaxy Watches is usually one to two days, much shorter than Huawei or Amazfit. If that matters more to you than smart features, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-30000-nepal\">smartwatches under Rs 30,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/samsung-galaxy-watch-fe.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(73,20,'Samsung Tablet Price in Nepal (November 2026)','samsung-tablet-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Samsung\'s Galaxy Tabs run from simple family tablets to laptop replacements. In Nepal they cost from Rs 21,999 for the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-a11\">Galaxy Tab A11</a> to Rs 1,29,999 for the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s11\">Galaxy Tab S11</a>.</p>\n<h2>Samsung tablets price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-a11\">Samsung Galaxy Tab A11</a></td><td>WiFi</td><td>Rs 21,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>5G+WiFi</td><td>Rs 36,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s10-lite\">Samsung Galaxy Tab S10 lite</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 63,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s10-fe\">Samsung Galaxy Tab S10 FE</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 74,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s11\">Samsung Galaxy Tab S11</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,29,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our recommendations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>For kids and videos:</strong> the Tab A11 is affordable and has Samsung\'s long update support. There\'s a 5G version if you need data away from Wi-Fi.</li>\n<li><strong>For students who take notes:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s10-fe\">Tab S10 FE</a> (Rs 74,999) includes the S Pen in the box and is rated IP68. It\'s a great note-taking tablet. The <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s10-lite\">Tab S10 Lite</a> is a cheaper option with a pen.</li>\n<li><strong>To replace a laptop:</strong> the Tab S11 has an AMOLED screen and a Dimensity 9400+ chip, and DeX mode gives you a desktop-style layout with a keyboard.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compare with iPads and Xiaomi tablets in our <a href=\"/guides/best-tablets-nepal\">tablet guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/samsung-galaxy-tab-s11.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(74,20,'Sony Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','sony-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Sony makes some of the best noise-cancelling earbuds you can buy, and its flagship WF-1000X series is often the benchmark other brands are measured against. In Nepal, prices run from Rs 16,400 for the <a href=\"/products/sony-wf-c510\">WF-C510</a> to Rs 64,999 for the <a href=\"/products/sony-wf-1000xm6\">WF-1000XM6</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sony earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wf-c510\">Sony WF-C510</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 16,400</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wfc700n\">Sony WF‑C700N</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 28,500</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wf-1000xm5\">Sony WF-1000XM5</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 50,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wf-1000xm6\">Sony WF-1000XM6</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Sony earbuds?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Simple and light:</strong> the WF-C510. Sony sound with no noise cancellation, good for gym and everyday use.</li>\n<li><strong>Value with ANC:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/sony-wfc700n\">WF-C700N</a> (Rs 28,500) adds noise cancellation and multipoint in a small, comfortable design.</li>\n<li><strong>The best:</strong> the WF-1000XM6 has class-leading noise cancellation, LDAC and excellent call quality. It\'s worth it for frequent flyers and long bus journeys. The previous <a href=\"/products/sony-wf-1000xm5\">WF-1000XM5</a> is still excellent and costs about Rs 15,000 less.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Sony\'s prices in Nepal are high next to Soundcore and CMF, so compare features first. See also our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-20000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 20,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/sony-wf-1000xm6.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(75,20,'Sony Headphones Price in Nepal (November 2026)','sony-headphones-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Sony\'s over-ear headphones in Nepal cover three quite different groups of buyers: travellers who want the best noise cancellation, bass lovers, and gamers. Prices run from Rs 16,200 for the <a href=\"/products/sony-wh-g300-inzone-h3\">INZONE H3</a> gaming headset to Rs 1,06,900 for the special-edition <a href=\"/products/sony-1000x-the-collexion\">1000X The Collexion</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sony headphones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-g300-inzone-h3\">Sony WH-G300 INZONE H3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 16,200</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-ch720n\">Sony WH-CH720N</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 27,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-g500-inzone-h5\">Sony WH-G500 INZONE H5</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 28,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-ult900n-ult-wear\">Sony WH-ULT900N ULT WEAR</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 35,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-g900n-inzone-h9\">Sony WH-G900N INZONE H9</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 55,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-1000xm5\">Sony WH-1000XM5</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 57,600</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-wh-1000xm6\">Sony WH-1000XM6</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 88,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/sony-1000x-the-collexion\">Sony 1000X THE COLLEXION</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 1,06,900</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which Sony headphones?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>For travel and work:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/sony-wh-1000xm6\">WH-1000XM6</a> has some of the best noise cancellation and call quality available. The older <a href=\"/products/sony-wh-1000xm5\">WH-1000XM5</a> costs about Rs 31,000 less and is still excellent.</li>\n<li><strong>For bass:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/sony-wh-ult900n-ult-wear\">ULT Wear</a> (Rs 35,000) has a heavy, punchy sound, LDAC, multipoint and up to 50 hours of playback.</li>\n<li><strong>On a budget:</strong> the WH-CH720N is light and comfortable, with decent noise cancellation for its price.</li>\n<li><strong>For PC and PS5 gaming:</strong> the INZONE H3, H5 and H9 headsets have clear microphones and accurate positional sound.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Collexion is a luxury edition. It sounds great, but you\'re paying mostly for the materials. For more affordable noise cancellation, see <a href=\"/guides/best-headphones-under-30000-nepal\">headphones under Rs 30,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/sony-wh-1000xm5.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(76,20,'Tecno Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','tecno-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Tecno sells mostly budget phones in Nepal, and several of them offer screens or batteries you\'d normally pay more for. Prices run from Rs 11,499 for the <a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-go-2\">Spark Go 2</a> to Rs 65,999 for the <a href=\"/products/tecno-camon-slim\">Camon Slim</a>.</p>\n<h2>Tecno phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-go-2\">Tecno Spark Go 2</a></td><td>3GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 11,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 13,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 14,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-go-3\">Tecno Spark Go 3</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 21,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 25,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-50-4g\">Tecno Spark 50 4G</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 29,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 32,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-30\">Tecno Spark 30</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 29,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-40-pro\">Tecno Spark 40 Pro</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-pova-6\">Tecno Pova 6</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 44,990</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-50-pro\">Tecno Spark 50 Pro</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 47,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-pova-curve-2\">Tecno Pova Curve 2</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 52,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-pova-8\">Tecno Pova 8</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/tecno-camon-slim\">Tecno Camon Slim</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 65,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Worth a look</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best screen for the money:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-40-pro\">Spark 40 Pro</a> (Rs 33,999) has a 144Hz AMOLED and 45W charging. Few phones under Rs 35,000 match that display.</li>\n<li><strong>Battery and a curved screen:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/tecno-pova-curve-2\">Pova Curve 2</a> (Rs 52,999) has an 8,000mAh battery and a curved AMOLED.</li>\n<li><strong>Slim and light:</strong> the Camon Slim is for people who want a thin phone that still looks premium.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Spark Go models are very basic phones, so aim for at least 4GB/128GB. Tecno\'s software updates are shorter than Samsung\'s or Xiaomi\'s, so check that before buying a phone you\'ll keep for years. Compare with others in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-40000-nepal\">phones under Rs 40,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/tecno-spark-go-3.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(77,20,'Xiaomi Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','xiaomi-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Xiaomi sells its earbuds under the Redmi name in Nepal, and they\'re some of the best value around, especially at the low end. Prices run from Rs 1,999 for the <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-5a\">Redmi Buds 5A</a> to Rs 14,999 for the <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-pro\">Redmi Buds 8 Pro</a>.</p>\n<h2>Xiaomi earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-5a\">Redmi Buds 5A</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 1,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-6-play\">Redmi Buds 6 Play</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-active\">Redmi Buds 8 Active</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-lite\">Redmi Buds 8 Lite</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8\">Redmi Buds 8</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 10,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-pro\">Redmi Buds 8 Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 14,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Cheapest good pair:</strong> the Redmi Buds 5A. It\'s a great first pair of earbuds and costs less than a dinner out.</li>\n<li><strong>Best value with ANC:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-lite\">Redmi Buds 8 Lite</a> (Rs 4,999) and <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-active\">Buds 8 Active</a> add noise cancellation for under Rs 5,000.</li>\n<li><strong>The best Redmi earbuds:</strong> the Buds 8 Pro has strong noise cancellation, LDAC and multipoint. It competes with pairs costing twice as much.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you use a Xiaomi or Redmi phone, pairing and extra settings are a little easier, but these work fine with any phone. More options are in our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 5,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/redmi-buds-8-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(78,20,'Xiaomi Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','xiaomi-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Xiaomi, through its Redmi and POCO brands, sells more phone models in Nepal than almost anyone, from the Rs 20,499 <a href=\"/products/redmi-a7-4g\">Redmi A7</a> to the Rs 1,99,999 <a href=\"/products/xiaomi-17-ultra\">Xiaomi 17 Ultra</a>. The <strong>Redmi A and Redmi</strong> numbered phones are budget models, the <strong>Redmi Note</strong> series is the popular mid-range, <strong>POCO</strong> is performance for the money, and <strong>Xiaomi</strong>-branded phones are flagships.</p>\n<h2>Xiaomi phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-a7-4g\">Redmi A7 4G</a></td><td>3GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 20,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-a7-pro-4g\">Redmi A7 Pro 4G</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 21,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 23,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-15-4g\">Redmi 15 4G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 27,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 29,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-17-4g\">Redmi 17 4G</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 32,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 37,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-17-5g\">Redmi 17 5G</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 37,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 45,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-4g\">Redmi Note 15 4G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-pro-4g\">Redmi Note 15 Pro 4G</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 35,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-m8s\">POCO M8s</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 46,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-4g\">Redmi Note 17 4G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 42,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 47,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-5g\">Redmi Note 15 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 43,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 49,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-5g\">Redmi Note 17 5G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 47,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 52,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-pro-5g\">Redmi Note 15 Pro 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 53,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 57,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-m8-pro\">POCO M8 Pro</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 58,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-x7-pro\">Poco X7 Pro</a></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-pro-plus\">Redmi Note 15 Pro Plus 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 63,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-15t\">Xiaomi 15T</a></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 64,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-max-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro Max 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 79,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-f7\">Poco F7</a></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-x8-pro\">Poco X8 Pro</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 76,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-17t\">Xiaomi 17T</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 92,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 99,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-x8-pro-max\">Poco X8 Pro Max</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 94,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,04,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/poco-f8-pro\">Poco F8 Pro</a></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,04,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-17-ultra\">Xiaomi 17 Ultra</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,99,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Budget 5G:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/redmi-17-5g\">Redmi 17 5G</a> (from Rs 33,999) has a huge battery and a smooth 120Hz screen.</li>\n<li><strong>Value:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/poco-m8s\">POCO M8s</a> (from Rs 39,999) pairs a 7,000mAh battery with a 120Hz AMOLED.</li>\n<li><strong>The Note series:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-max-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro Max</a> has a 10,000mAh battery and 100W charging. Read <a href=\"/reviews/redmi-note-17-pro-max-review-nepal\">our review</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance for less:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/poco-x8-pro-max\">POCO X8 Pro Max</a> (Rs 94,999) has an 8,500mAh battery and a Dimensity 9500s, flagship speed for under a lakh.</li>\n<li><strong>Camera flagship:</strong> the Xiaomi 17 Ultra, with Leica-tuned cameras.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Xiaomi often sells the same phone in 4G and 5G versions with similar names, such as the Redmi 17 4G and Redmi 17 5G. Check which one you\'re paying for.</p>','gadgets/2026/poco-x8-pro-max.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(79,20,'Xiaomi Smartwatch Price in Nepal (November 2026)','xiaomi-smartwatch-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Xiaomi\'s watches, mostly under the Redmi name, are a popular first smartwatch in Nepal: cheap, light and long-lasting. Prices run from Rs 4,499 for the <a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-5-active\">Redmi Watch 5 Active</a> to Rs 39,999 for the <a href=\"/products/xiaomi-watch-s5\">Xiaomi Watch S5</a>.</p>\n<h2>Xiaomi smartwatches price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-5-active\">Redmi Watch 5 Active</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-active\">Redmi Watch 6 Active</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 10,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-lite\">Redmi Watch 6 Lite</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 14,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6\">Redmi Watch 6</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 20,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-watch-s5\">Xiaomi Watch S5</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Which one?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>First smartwatch:</strong> the Redmi Watch 5 Active covers steps, heart rate, notifications and Bluetooth calling for very little money.</li>\n<li><strong>Our pick:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6\">Redmi Watch 6</a> (Rs 20,499) has an AMOLED screen and built-in GPS, and lasts up to about 12 days of normal use. That\'s a lot of watch for the price.</li>\n<li><strong>The more premium one:</strong> the Xiaomi Watch S5 has a round, classic design and better materials.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-active\">Watch 6 Active</a> and <a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-lite\">Watch 6 Lite</a> sit in between. If you run outdoors, choose a model with built-in GPS so you don\'t need to carry your phone. Compare brands in our <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-30000-nepal\">smartwatches under Rs 30,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/redmi-watch-6.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(80,20,'Xiaomi Tablet Price in Nepal (November 2026)','xiaomi-tablet-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Xiaomi\'s tablets are some of the best value in Nepal, especially the Redmi Pads for videos and online classes. Prices run from Rs 25,999 for the <a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2-9-7\">Redmi Pad 2 9.7</a> to Rs 59,999 for the <a href=\"/products/xiaomi-pad-8\">Xiaomi Pad 8</a>.</p>\n<h2>Xiaomi tablets price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2-9-7\">Redmi Pad 2 9.7</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 25,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2\">Redmi Pad 2 11-inch</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 29,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 34,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-pad-7\">Xiaomi Pad 7</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 44,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 49,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-pad-8\">Xiaomi Pad 8</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 59,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 69,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>For most families:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2\">Redmi Pad 2 (11-inch)</a>, from Rs 29,999. Its 2.5K screen, quad speakers and big battery make it hard to beat for watching and studying. Choose the 8GB/256GB version if you can.</li>\n<li><strong>For students and creative work:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/xiaomi-pad-7\">Xiaomi Pad 7</a> (from Rs 44,999) has a sharp 3.2K 144Hz screen and a Snapdragon 7+ Gen 3. It\'s the best performance under Rs 50,000.</li>\n<li><strong>The fastest:</strong> the Pad 8 steps up to a Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 and a 9,200mAh battery.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The 9.7-inch Redmi Pad 2 is smaller and lighter, a good size for children. See also our <a href=\"/guides/best-tablets-nepal\">tablet guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/xiaomi-pad-8.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(81,20,'ZTE Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','zte-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>ZTE, mainly through its <strong>nubia</strong> brand, sells affordable phones in Nepal, all under Rs 41,000. Prices run from Rs 15,999 for the <a href=\"/products/zte-a37e\">ZTE A37e</a> to Rs 40,999 for the <a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-neo-3-5g\">Nubia Neo 3 5G</a>.</p>\n<h2>ZTE phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-a37e\">ZTE A37e</a></td><td>3GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 15,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-a57\">ZTE Nubia A57</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 18,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 24,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-a36\">ZTE Nubia A36</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 18,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-a56\">ZTE Nubia A56</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 19,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-a77\">ZTE Nubia A77</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 25,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-v80-max\">ZTE Nubia V80 Max</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 29,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 31,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-v80-design\">ZTE Nubia V80 Design</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 29,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 32,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-air\">ZTE nubia Air</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-neo-3-5g\">ZTE Nubia Neo 3 5G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 40,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Worth a look</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Best overall:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-air\">nubia Air</a> (Rs 33,999) has a 120Hz AMOLED screen and IP68 water resistance in a slim body. That\'s unusual protection at this price.</li>\n<li><strong>For mobile gamers:</strong> the Nubia Neo 3 5G has a gaming-focused design and shoulder triggers.</li>\n<li><strong>The V80 series:</strong> the V80 Max and V80 Design are big-screen budget phones with 8GB of RAM.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The A-series phones at the bottom of the list are basic, and the 64GB versions fill up quickly. Compare with better-known brands in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-25000-nepal\">phones under Rs 25,000</a> guide, where Samsung and Realme offer longer software support.</p>','gadgets/2026/zte-a37e.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(82,20,'boAt Earbuds Price in Nepal (November 2026)','boat-earbuds-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>boAt is one of the biggest budget audio brands in South Asia, and in Nepal its earbuds cost between Rs 2,199 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-212\">Airdopes 212</a> and Rs 6,699 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion-anc-pro\">Nirvana Ion ANC Pro</a>. The range is huge and the names are confusing, so here\'s how to make sense of it.</p>\n<h2>boAt earbuds price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-212\">boAt Airdopes 212</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,199</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-alpha-gen-2\">boAt Airdopes Alpha Gen 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-91-prime\">boAt Airdopes 91 Prime</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-131-gen-2\">boAt Airdopes 131 Gen 2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-111-v2\">boAt Airdopes 111 v2</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,699</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-immortal-131\">boAt Immortal 131</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,799</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-121-pro-plus\">boAt Airdopes 121 Pro Plus</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-120\">boAt Airdopes 120</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-alpha\">boAt Airdopes Alpha</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,099</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-161-anc-elite\">boAt Airdopes 161 ANC Elite</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,199</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-131-elite\">boAt Airdopes 131 Elite ANC</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,199</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-supreme\">boAt Airdopes Supreme</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,449</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion\">boAt Nirvana Ion</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-800-hi-def\">boAt Airdopes 800 HI-DEF</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-loop\">boAt Airdopes Loop</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-iris\">boAt Nirvana Iris</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 4,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-space\">boAt Nirvana Space</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,099</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-crystl\">boAt Nirvana Crystl</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,199</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-411-anc\">boAt Airdopes 411 ANC</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ivy\">boAt Nirvana Ivy</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,899</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-flex-454-anc\">boAt Airdopes Flex 454 ANC</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-x-tws\">boAt Nirvana X TWS</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion-anc\">boAt Nirvana Ion ANC</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,599</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion-anc-pro\">boAt Nirvana Ion ANC Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,699</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>How to choose</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Airdopes (under Rs 3,500):</strong> everyday earbuds with a bass-forward sound and long battery life. Fine for calls and music. Models labelled \"ANC\" add basic noise cancellation.</li>\n<li><strong>Immortal:</strong> boAt\'s gaming line, with low-latency modes for mobile games.</li>\n<li><strong>Nirvana (Rs 4,000–6,700):</strong> the better-sounding range. The <a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion-anc\">Nirvana Ion ANC</a> pairs noise cancellation with very long battery life, up to about 120 hours with the case.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>boAt\'s strength is battery life and price, not sound quality or call clarity. At Rs 4,000–5,000, also compare the <a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-buds-4\">OnePlus Nord Buds 4</a> and <a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200\">Realme Buds T200</a> in our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 5,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-nirvana-ion-anc.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(83,20,'boAt Headphones Price in Nepal (November 2026)','boat-headphones-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>boAt\'s Rockerz headphones are among the cheapest wireless over-ear options in Nepal, from Rs 2,299 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-371\">Rockerz 371</a> to Rs 6,299 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-650-pro\">Rockerz 650 Pro</a>.</p>\n<h2>boAt headphones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-371\">boAt Rockerz 371</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-411\">boAt Rockerz 411</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,799</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-430\">boAt Rockerz 430</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-412\">boAt Rockerz 412</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,099</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-650-pro\">boAt Rockerz 650 Pro</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,299</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What to buy</h2>\n<p>If you can spend the extra, the <strong>Rockerz 650 Pro</strong> is the clear pick. It supports multipoint, so it stays connected to your phone and laptop together, and lasts up to about 80 hours on a charge. That\'s great for students who use one pair for classes and music.</p>\n<p>The Rockerz 371, 411, 412 and 430 are simple, bass-heavy headphones for home and travel. None of them has noise cancellation, and they feel lighter-built than pricier brands.</p>\n<p>If you want noise cancellation without spending much more, look at the <a href=\"/products/soundcore-q11i\">Soundcore Q11i</a> and other picks in our <a href=\"/guides/best-headphones-under-5000-nepal\">headphones under Rs 5,000</a> and <a href=\"/guides/best-headphones-under-10000-nepal\">under Rs 10,000</a> guides.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-rockerz-650-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(84,20,'boAt Smartwatch Price in Nepal (November 2026)','boat-smartwatch-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>boAt\'s smartwatches are some of the cheapest in Nepal, with prices between Rs 2,999 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-wave-fury\">Wave Fury</a> and Rs 6,799 for the <a href=\"/products/boat-ultima-ember\">Ultima Ember</a>. They\'re popular as a first smartwatch, or as a gift.</p>\n<h2>boAt smartwatches price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-wave-fury\">boAt Wave Fury</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 2,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-wave-call-3\">boAt Wave Call 3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,199</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-wave-sigma-3\">boAt Wave Sigma 3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,299</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-storm-call-3-plus\">boAt Storm Call 3 Plus</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,399</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-wave-astra-3\">boAt Wave Astra 3</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 3,399</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-enigma-oreon\">boAt Enigma Orion</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 5,699</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-ultima-regal\">boAt Ultima Regal</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,099</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-enigma-radiant\">boAt Enigma Radiant</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,799</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/boat-ultima-ember\">boAt Ultima Ember</a></td><td>Standard</td><td>Rs 6,799</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>What you get</h2>\n<p>All of them show notifications, count steps and track heart rate, and most support Bluetooth calling, so you can answer calls from your wrist when the phone is in your bag. The <strong>Wave</strong> and <strong>Storm</strong> models are the cheapest, with square screens. The <strong>Enigma</strong> and <strong>Ultima</strong> models look more like traditional watches, with round or AMOLED screens.</p>\n<p>Our pick is the <a href=\"/products/boat-ultima-regal\">Ultima Regal</a> (Rs 6,099). Its AMOLED screen is easy to read outdoors, and it lasts up to about a week.</p>\n<p>Keep your expectations in check. These watches don\'t have built-in GPS, and the health readings are rough estimates. For accurate fitness tracking, the <a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-5-active\">Redmi Watch 5 Active</a> and Amazfit models in our <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-10000-nepal\">smartwatches under Rs 10,000</a> guide are better.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-ultima-regal.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(85,20,'vivo Mobile Price in Nepal (November 2026)','vivo-phone-price-in-nepal','buying-guide','<p>vivo sells phones across every budget in Nepal, from the Rs 19,999 <a href=\"/products/vivo-y05e\">Y05e</a> to the Rs 1,99,999 <a href=\"/products/vivo-x300-pro\">X300 Pro</a>. The <strong>Y series</strong> covers budget phones with big batteries, the <strong>V series</strong> is mid-range with slim designs and good selfie cameras, and the <strong>X series</strong> is camera-focused flagships.</p>\n<h2>vivo phones price list</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Variant</th><th>Price in Nepal</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y05e\">Vivo Y05e</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 19,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y05\">Vivo Y05</a></td><td>4GB/64GB</td><td>Rs 24,974</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 28,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y31d\">Vivo Y31d</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 32,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 37,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 43,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 51,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y11d\">Vivo Y11d</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y32\">Vivo Y32</a></td><td>4GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 39,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 45,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>6GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 52,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y21-5g\">Vivo Y21 5G</a></td><td>6GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 40,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v60-lite-4g\">Vivo V60 Lite 4G</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 43,499</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v60-lite-5g\">Vivo V60 Lite 5G</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 51,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-y500\">Vivo Y500</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 54,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 61,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v70-fe\">Vivo V70 FE</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 62,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 72,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v80-lite-5g\">Vivo V80 Lite</a></td><td>8GB/128GB</td><td>Rs 63,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 73,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v60-5g\">Vivo V60</a></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 74,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 79,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v70\">Vivo V70</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 84,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,02,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>12GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,22,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-v80\">vivo V80</a></td><td>8GB/256GB</td><td>Rs 1,08,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>8GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,33,999</td></tr>\n<tr><td><a href=\"/products/vivo-x300-pro\">vivo X300 Pro</a></td><td>16GB/512GB</td><td>Rs 1,99,999</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Tough and long-lasting:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/vivo-y32\">vivo Y32</a> (from Rs 39,999) has an 8,000mAh battery and IP68 water resistance, a combination that\'s hard to find at this price.</li>\n<li><strong>Slim mid-ranger:</strong> the <a href=\"/products/vivo-v80-lite-5g\">V80 Lite</a> is a light phone with a good selfie camera, popular for social media.</li>\n<li><strong>Camera flagship:</strong> the X300 Pro is one of the best camera phones on sale in Nepal. It costs less than the Galaxy S26 Ultra, and its zoom is excellent.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cheapest Y-series models start at 4GB/64GB, so pick a 128GB version. The X300 Pro went up in price in September 2026, as covered in <a href=\"/news/why-gadget-prices-rose-nepal-2026\">why gadget prices rose this year</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/vivo-x300-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(86,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 15,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-15000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 15,000 you\'re buying a phone for calls, WhatsApp, Facebook and YouTube, and that\'s fine, as long as you know what you\'re giving up. Every phone at this price uses an entry-level chip and a basic screen.</p>\n<h2>The few worth considering</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/tecno-spark-go-2\">Tecno Spark Go 2</a>: from Rs 11,499. The cheapest phone here with a reasonable chip (Unisoc T7250). Pick the 4GB/128GB version at Rs 14,999 if you can.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/infinix-smart-10\">Infinix Smart 10</a>: Rs 14,999. The same chip as the Spark Go 2, in a slightly more modern design.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/blackview-wave-10c\">Blackview Wave 10C</a>: from Rs 14,499. A simple, sturdy everyday phone.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/ai-plus-plus\">Ai+ Pulse</a>: Rs 14,999. Worth a look if you find it in a shop near you.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Honest advice</h2>\n<p>Storage is the biggest trap at this price. A 32GB or 64GB phone fills up with WhatsApp photos within months. If you can add a few thousand rupees, the phones in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-20000-nepal\">under Rs 20,000</a> and <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-25000-nepal\">under Rs 25,000</a> guides are a noticeable step up and will last longer. As a backup phone or a first phone for a child, though, these do the job.</p>','gadgets/2026/infinix-smart-10.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(87,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 20,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-20000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 15,000–20,000 buys a decent everyday phone with enough storage to last. The chips are still entry-level, so these are phones for messaging, social media, video and calls rather than gaming.</p>\n<h2>Our shortlist</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/infinix-smart-10-plus\">Infinix Smart 10 Plus</a>: Rs 15,999. 4GB/128GB for the price of most 64GB phones. A sensible pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-note-70\">Realme Note 70</a>: from Rs 16,999. A dependable everyday phone from a brand with a big service network.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/honor-choice-t10\">Honor Choice T10</a>: from Rs 16,499. Choose the 4GB/64GB version or above.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/zte-nubia-a57\">ZTE Nubia A57</a>: from Rs 18,999. Pick the 128GB version.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/vivo-y05e\">vivo Y05e</a>: Rs 19,999. A big battery and vivo\'s wide after-sales network.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What to check before paying</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>128GB storage</strong> if at all possible.</li>\n<li><strong>Charging speed:</strong> many phones here charge slowly at 10–15W. Plan on charging overnight.</li>\n<li><strong>That it\'s official.</strong> Here\'s <a href=\"/guides/how-to-check-phone-is-official-in-nepal\">how to check</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Stretching to Rs 21,000–25,000 gets you faster charging and better screens. See our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-25000-nepal\">phones under Rs 25,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/infinix-smart-10-plus.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(88,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 30,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-30000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 20,000–30,000 is where budget phones start to feel genuinely good. You\'ll find bigger batteries, 120Hz screens and, at the top of the range, AMOLED displays.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/infinix-note-50x\">Infinix Note 50x</a>: Rs 21,999. The fastest chip at this price (Dimensity 7300 Ultimate), a great choice for light gaming.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/infinix-hot-50-pro-plus\">Infinix Hot 50 Pro Plus</a>: Rs 25,999. A 120Hz AMOLED screen and 8GB/256GB. A lovely screen for the money.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-15-4g\">Redmi 15 4G</a>: from Rs 27,999. A 7,000mAh battery for people who hate charging.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oppo-a6c\">OPPO A6c</a>: from Rs 24,999. Another 7,000mAh battery, though charging is slow.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a07\">Samsung Galaxy A07</a>: from Rs 25,499. The safe brand choice, with long software support.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/blackview-fort-1\">Blackview Fort 1</a> (Rs 21,999) is a rugged alternative with IP68 and a 10,000mAh battery, if you need toughness more than looks.</p>\n<p>Remember that most phones in this range are 4G. That\'s fine on NTC and Ncell today, as we explain in <a href=\"/news/ntc-ncell-5g-rollout-nepal-2024\">our 5G explainer</a>. For a 5G phone, see <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-40000-nepal\">under Rs 40,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/redmi-15-4g.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(89,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 50,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-50000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 35,000–50,000 is the busiest part of the Nepali phone market, and the competition shows. Phones here routinely have AMOLED screens, 120Hz refresh rates and OIS cameras, and some even have IP68 water resistance.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/infinix-note-50s\">Infinix Note 50s</a>: Rs 35,999. The value pick, with an AMOLED screen, a fast Dimensity 7300 Ultimate and OIS for under Rs 36,000.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/poco-m8s\">POCO M8s</a>: from Rs 39,999. A 7,000mAh battery and a 120Hz AMOLED.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-m36-5g\">Samsung Galaxy M36 5G</a>: from Rs 41,999. Samsung\'s software and update promise, with an OIS camera.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/moto-g96\">Motorola Moto G96 5G</a>: Rs 44,999. IP68 and a clean Android experience.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-14-5g\">Realme 14 5G</a>: Rs 49,999. IP68, OIS and a 120Hz AMOLED at the top of the budget.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a17-5g\">Galaxy A17 5G</a> (from Rs 44,999) and <a href=\"/products/redmi-note-15-5g\">Redmi Note 15 5G</a> are also strong choices. In this range, pick on what matters to you: battery, screen, or how long you\'ll get software updates.</p>','gadgets/2026/realme-14-5g.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(90,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 70,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-70000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>At Rs 55,000–70,000 you can buy a phone that\'s close to flagship speed. Several models here use chips from the top tier, and many add IP68 water resistance.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/poco-f7\">POCO F7</a>: Rs 69,999. A Snapdragon 8s Gen 4 and IP68, the fastest phone at this price.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/poco-x8-pro\">POCO X8 Pro</a>: Rs 69,999. The Dimensity 8500 Ultra and IP68, an alternative to the F7.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-ce-5\">OnePlus Nord CE5</a>: Rs 59,999. A 7,100mAh battery and OxygenOS, a smooth, long-lasting phone.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-note-17-pro-max-5g\">Redmi Note 17 Pro Max</a>: Rs 69,999. A 10,000mAh battery and 100W charging.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/vivo-v70-fe\">vivo V70 FE</a>: from Rs 62,999. A slim design with a 7,000mAh battery.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If cameras matter most, the <a href=\"/products/nothing-phone-4a\">Nothing Phone 4a</a> (Rs 69,999) has a periscope zoom, rare at this price. For Samsung fans, the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-a37-5g\">Galaxy A37 5G</a> costs a little more but gets long software support.</p>','gadgets/2026/poco-f7.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(91,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 1,00,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-100000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Just under a lakh is where \"flagship killers\" live: phones with top-tier chips and huge batteries that cost half what the big-name flagships do.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-15r\">OnePlus 15R</a>: from Rs 98,499. Flagship-level speed for under a lakh, and our pick for most people at this budget.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/poco-x8-pro-max\">POCO X8 Pro Max</a>: Rs 94,999. An 8,500mAh battery and the Dimensity 9500s.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-6\">OnePlus Nord 6</a>: Rs 89,999. A 7,500mAh battery and a Snapdragon 8s Gen 4.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-p4-power\">Realme P4 Power</a>: Rs 76,999. A 10,001mAh battery. It\'ll last two days of heavy use.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/honor-600\">Honor 600</a>: from Rs 84,999. A good-looking phone with a strong camera.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Spending this much, it\'s worth checking software support. Samsung, Google and OnePlus promise more years of updates than most. If you can stretch, the <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-fe\">Galaxy S26 FE</a> is covered in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-under-150000-nepal\">under Rs 1,50,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/poco-x8-pro-max.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(92,20,'Best Phones Under Rs 1,50,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-phones-under-150000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Between one lakh and one and a half lakh, you\'re choosing between the best of the \"value flagships\" and the cheaper models from the big brands.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/poco-f8-pro\">POCO F8 Pro</a>: Rs 1,04,999. A Snapdragon 8 Elite and IP68 for just over a lakh. The speed-per-rupee pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26-fe\">Samsung Galaxy S26 FE</a>: Rs 1,24,999. A Samsung flagship design, IP68 and long software support.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/google-pixel-10\">Google Pixel 10</a>: Rs 1,28,000. Google\'s camera and clean software.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oppo-find-x9-pro\">OPPO Find X9 Pro</a>: Rs 1,25,999. A 7,500mAh battery and the Dimensity 9500, a serious flagship for the money.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/honor-600-pro\">Honor 600 Pro</a>: from Rs 1,29,999. A Snapdragon 8 Elite and a 7,000mAh battery.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Compact phone fans should look at the <a href=\"/products/oneplus-13s\">OnePlus 13s</a> (Rs 1,19,999). The <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-s26\">Galaxy S26</a> (Rs 1,39,999) is the smallest current Samsung flagship. For the absolute best, see the flagships in our <a href=\"/guides/best-phones-in-nepal-by-budget\">phones by budget</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/poco-x8-pro-max.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(93,20,'Best Laptops Under Rs 80,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-laptops-under-80000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 80,000 you can still buy a perfectly good laptop for school, college and office work, as long as you avoid the weakest chips.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/asus-vivobook-15-x1504va-2023-intel-core-i5-1334u-16gb-512gb-156-fhd\">ASUS Vivobook 15 X1504VA</a>: Rs 79,999. A Core i5 and 16GB of RAM. The memory makes it the one most likely to stay usable for years.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/acer-aspire-go-15-ag15-21pt-2024-ryzen-5-7520u\">Acer Aspire Go 15 (Ryzen 5 7520U)</a>: Rs 76,000. A capable 4-core chip for study and office work.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/dell-15-dc15250-2025\">Dell 15 DC15250</a>: from Rs 78,999. Simple and well supported, with a 120Hz screen.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/lenovo-ideapad-slim-3-14amn8-2023\">Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 3 14AMN8</a>: Rs 66,999. Light and cheap, for light work only.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What to avoid</h2>\n<p>Laptops with Intel Celeron or N100 chips and 4GB of RAM, such as the Dell Wyse 5470 at the bottom of this range, are frustratingly slow on modern Windows. And remember that 8GB of RAM is fine for now but tight for the future. If you can reach a lakh, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-laptops-under-100000-nepal\">laptops under Rs 1,00,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/asus-vivobook-15-x1504va-2023-intel-core-i5-1334u-16gb-512gb-156-fhd.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(94,20,'Best Laptops Under Rs 1,00,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-laptops-under-100000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>A lakh is the budget we\'d suggest for a laptop you want to keep for four or five years. It\'s enough for 16GB of RAM, a decent processor and a 512GB SSD.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/msi-modern-14-2024-intel-core-7-150u\">MSI Modern 14 F1MG</a>: Rs 93,000. In its Core 7 150U configuration with 16GB and 1TB, it\'s excellent value.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/acer-aspire-lite-15-al15-41-2024-ryzen-5-7430u\">Acer Aspire Lite 15 (Ryzen 5 7430U)</a>: Rs 97,999. A 6-core Ryzen and 16GB.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/hp-15-fc0043nq-2024\">HP 15 (Ryzen 5 7520U)</a>: from Rs 90,999. Pick the 16GB version.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/asus-zenbook-14-oled-q415\">ASUS Zenbook 14 OLED Q415</a>: Rs 89,999. An OLED screen and Core Ultra 5 125H at this price is rare, but it only has 8GB of RAM.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Also worth a look: the <a href=\"/products/dell-pro-15-pv15255-2025\">Dell Pro 15</a> with a 120Hz screen, and the <a href=\"/products/asus-vivobook-15-x1504va-2023-intel-core-i5-1334u-16gb-512gb-156-fhd\">Vivobook 15 X1504VA</a> if you want to save Rs 15,000–20,000.</p>\n<p>None of these are for gaming or heavy video work. For that, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-gaming-laptops-nepal\">gaming laptop guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/hp-15-fc0043nq-2024.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(95,20,'Best Laptops Under Rs 1,50,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-laptops-under-150000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>At Rs 1–1.5 lakh, laptops split into two groups. Thin, efficient machines with long battery life suit students and professionals, while entry gaming laptops have dedicated graphics. Decide which you need first.</p>\n<h2>For work and study</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/acer-aspire-ai-a14-52mt-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-258v\">Acer Aspire 14 AI (Core Ultra 7 258V)</a>: Rs 1,39,999. 32GB of RAM, 1TB and long battery life. Hard to beat.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/hp-probook-445-g11-ryzen-5-7535u\">HP ProBook 445 G11</a>: Rs 1,14,999, and <a href=\"/products/hp-elitebook-655-g10-ryzen-5-pro-7530u\">EliteBook 655 G10</a>: Rs 1,29,999. Business laptops with 32GB of RAM.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/asus-vivobook-s15-oled-x-plus-16gb-1tb-15-6-3k-oled\">ASUS Vivobook S15 (Snapdragon X Plus)</a>: Rs 1,42,800. An OLED screen and outstanding battery life, but <a href=\"/news/qualcomm-oryon-snapdragon-x-elite-laptops-nepal-battery-benchmarks\">check app compatibility</a> first.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/acer-swift-lite-14-ai-sfl14-54m-786p-2025-intel-core-ultra-7-155u-16gb-512gb-14-wuxga-oled-60hz\">Acer Swift Lite 14 AI</a>: Rs 1,44,999. A light laptop with an OLED screen.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>For gaming</h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/hp-victus-15\">HP Victus 15</a> (from Rs 1,49,000) is the main option. Pick the RTX 4050 version. Our news piece on <a href=\"/news/best-gaming-laptops-nepal-under-150000-2024\">gaming laptops under Rs 1.5 lakh</a> covers the alternatives.</p>','gadgets/2026/dell-14-plus-2-in-1-db04255-2025-ryzen-ai-7-350-16gb-1tb-14-fhd.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(96,20,'Best Laptops Under Rs 2,00,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-laptops-under-200000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Up to Rs 2 lakh, you can choose between a capable gaming laptop and a premium thin-and-light.</p>\n<h2>For gaming</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/lenovo-loq-15-2025\">Lenovo LOQ 15 (2025)</a>: Rs 1,94,999. An RTX 5050 at a full 100W and a 100% sRGB screen. Our top value pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/asus-tuf-gaming-a16-fa607nuq-2026\">ASUS TUF A16</a>: Rs 1,83,999. An RTX 4050 and an 8-core Ryzen 7 170 in a sturdy 16-inch body.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/asus-tuf-gaming-f16-fx607-2024\">ASUS TUF F16 FX607</a>: from Rs 1,65,600. A cheaper TUF with a 16-inch screen.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>For work</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/acer-aspire-14-ai-a14-52mt-94h5-2025-intel-core-ultra-9-288v-32gb-1tb-14-wuxga-touch\">Acer Aspire 14 AI (Ultra 9 288V)</a>: Rs 1,84,999. 32GB of RAM, a touchscreen and excellent battery life.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/dell-inspiron-14-plus-7440-intel-core-ultra-9-185h\">Dell Inspiron 14 Plus 7440</a>: Rs 1,74,999. A powerful 14-inch for developers.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/hp-spectre-x360-14-eu0060ca-2024-intel-core-ultra-5-125h-16gb-16gb-14-3k-oled-touch\">HP Spectre x360 14</a>: Rs 1,64,999. A premium 2-in-1 with a 3K OLED.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/macbook-neo\">MacBook Neo</a> (from Rs 1,34,999) is also in this range if you\'d rather have a Mac. See our <a href=\"/guides/best-laptops-nepal-students-gamers\">best laptops guide</a> for higher budgets.</p>','gadgets/2026/asus-tuf-gaming-f16-fx607-2024.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(97,20,'Best Earbuds Under Rs 3,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-earbuds-under-3000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>You can get surprisingly good earbuds for under Rs 3,000 in Nepal, some even with noise cancellation. Expect bass-heavy sound and basic microphones, but long battery life.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/kick-phantom-buds-x-pro\">Kick Phantom Buds X Pro</a>: Rs 2,599. Noise cancellation and multipoint, a rare combination under Rs 3,000. Our top pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-5a\">Redmi Buds 5A</a>: Rs 1,999. The cheapest good pair, from a brand with a big service network.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200x\">Realme Buds T200x</a>: Rs 2,999. ANC and multipoint, with up to about 48 hours of battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-212\">boAt Airdopes 212</a>: Rs 2,199. Long battery life, up to around 75 hours with the case.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/anker-soundcore-p20i\">Soundcore P20i</a> (Rs 2,999) is another solid choice with a good app. At this price, fit matters more than features. Try the different ear tips in the box for a better seal and fuller sound. For better noise cancellation, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 5,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-airdopes-212.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(98,20,'Best Earbuds Under Rs 5,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 3,000–5,000 is the sweet spot for most people buying earbuds in Nepal. It\'s enough for real noise cancellation, multipoint and a decent app, and it\'s cheap enough that a lost earbud isn\'t a disaster.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-nord-buds-4\">OnePlus Nord Buds 4</a>: Rs 4,999. Good noise cancellation, multipoint and a reliable app. Our top pick for most people.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-t200\">Realme Buds T200</a>: Rs 4,499. ANC, LDAC and multipoint, the most features for the money.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-p30i\">Soundcore P30i</a>: Rs 4,999. Solid ANC and a case that doubles as a phone stand.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/kick-phantom-buds-x-pro\">Kick Phantom Buds X Pro</a>: Rs 2,599. If you\'d rather spend less, it still has ANC and multipoint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Also worth a look: the <a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-lite\">Redmi Buds 8 Lite</a> (Rs 4,999), and the <a href=\"/products/boat-airdopes-800-hi-def\">boAt Airdopes 800 HI-DEF</a> (Rs 4,299) for very long battery life.</p>\n<p>A tip: multipoint is worth having if you join calls on your laptop. The earbuds stay connected to the laptop and your phone at the same time. For stronger noise cancellation, step up to <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-10000-nepal\">under Rs 10,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/oneplus-nord-buds-4.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(99,20,'Best Earbuds Under Rs 10,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-earbuds-under-10000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 10,000, noise cancellation gets noticeably better and features like LDAC become common. This is good territory for daily commuters and anyone who takes a lot of calls.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-2-plus\">CMF Buds 2 Plus</a>: Rs 8,999. Strong ANC, LDAC and multipoint. The best all-rounder at this price.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-pro-2\">CMF Buds Pro 2</a>: Rs 9,599. The step-up CMF, with even better noise cancellation and a clever case dial.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-buds-air-8\">Realme Buds Air 8</a>: Rs 8,499. Comfortable, with good ANC and long battery life.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/anker-soundcore-r60i-nc\">Soundcore R60i NC</a>: Rs 5,499. ANC, LDAC and multipoint for barely more than budget pairs.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-nirvana-ion-anc\">boAt Nirvana Ion ANC</a>: Rs 6,599. For battery life above all, at up to about 120 hours with the case.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you use an iPhone, LDAC won\'t help, because iPhones use AAC, so choose on noise cancellation and fit instead. Under Rs 5,000? See <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">our cheaper picks</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-nirvana-ion-anc.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(100,20,'Best Earbuds Under Rs 20,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-earbuds-under-20000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 10,000–20,000 gets you close to flagship earbuds: strong noise cancellation, good call quality and premium sound, without Sony or Apple prices.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-liberty-5\">Soundcore Liberty 5</a>: Rs 17,499. Excellent ANC, LDAC and multipoint. Our top pick at this budget.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8-pro\">Redmi Buds 8 Pro</a>: Rs 14,999. Nearly as good for less, and a great match for Xiaomi phone owners.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/anker-soundcore-liberty-4-nc\">Soundcore Liberty 4 NC</a>: Rs 12,999. Older, but its noise cancellation is still very good, and the price has come down.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-buds-8\">Redmi Buds 8</a>: Rs 10,499. The cheapest way into this tier.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Don\'t overlook the <a href=\"/products/cmf-buds-pro-2\">CMF Buds Pro 2</a> (Rs 9,599) just below this budget. It\'s surprisingly close in performance. Samsung phone owners should also compare the <a href=\"/guides/samsung-earbuds-price-in-nepal\">Galaxy Buds</a> for the extra features they get with a Galaxy phone.</p>','gadgets/2026/soundcore-liberty-5.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(101,20,'Best Headphones Under Rs 5,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-headphones-under-5000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>There aren\'t many over-ear headphones under Rs 5,000 in Nepal, and none of them have proper noise cancellation. What you can get is comfortable wireless headphones with very long battery life, fine for music at home and online classes.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-q11i\">Soundcore Q11i</a>: Rs 4,999. The best-sounding pair here, with multipoint and up to about 60 hours of battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-412\">boAt Rockerz 412</a>: Rs 3,099. Multipoint and long battery life for little money.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-371\">boAt Rockerz 371</a>: Rs 2,299. The cheapest decent pair.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Over-ear headphones are often more comfortable than earbuds for long study sessions, and they don\'t fall out. If you need noise cancellation, though, earbuds give you more for the money at this price. See our <a href=\"/guides/best-earbuds-under-5000-nepal\">earbuds under Rs 5,000</a>. Or stretch to the headphones in our <a href=\"/guides/best-headphones-under-10000-nepal\">under Rs 10,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/soundcore-q11i.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(102,20,'Best Headphones Under Rs 10,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-headphones-under-10000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 10,000 you can buy well-built wireless headphones from JBL and Soundcore with excellent battery life. Strong noise cancellation is still mostly found above this price, though.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/jbl-tune-530bt\">JBL Tune 530BT</a>: Rs 9,500. Up to about 76 hours of battery and multipoint, with JBL\'s punchy sound.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-q20i\">Soundcore Q20i</a>: Rs 9,199. Adds hybrid noise cancellation, the cheapest decent ANC headphones here.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-rockerz-650-pro\">boAt Rockerz 650 Pro</a>: Rs 6,299. Multipoint and up to about 80 hours of battery for much less.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-q11i\">Soundcore Q11i</a>: Rs 4,999. If you want to save more.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <a href=\"/products/jbl-tune-530c\">JBL Tune 530C</a> uses a USB-C cable rather than Bluetooth, which is good for laptops, so check that your device supports USB-C audio. For proper noise cancellation for travel, see <a href=\"/guides/best-headphones-under-30000-nepal\">headphones under Rs 30,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/boat-rockerz-650-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(103,20,'Best Headphones Under Rs 30,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-headphones-under-30000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 15,000–30,000 is where noise-cancelling headphones get genuinely good. Buses, flights and noisy offices go quiet, and the sound quality improves too.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-space-q45\">Soundcore Space Q45</a>: Rs 19,999. Strong ANC, LDAC, multipoint and up to 65 hours of battery. Our value pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/nothing-headphone-a\">Nothing Headphone (a)</a>: Rs 26,999. A distinctive design with good ANC and LDAC.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/soundcore-space-2\">Soundcore Space 2</a>: Rs 24,499. Light and comfortable, with up to 70 hours of battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/cmf-headphone-pro\">CMF Headphone Pro</a>: Rs 13,999. Most of the features for much less.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/jbl-tune-780nc\">JBL Tune 780NC</a>: Rs 19,500. JBL\'s bass-heavy sound with noise cancellation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above this budget, the <a href=\"/products/sony-wh-1000xm5\">Sony WH-1000XM5</a> and XM6 offer the best noise cancellation around. See our <a href=\"/guides/sony-headphones-price-in-nepal\">Sony headphones guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/nothing-headphone-a.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(104,20,'Best Smartwatches Under Rs 5,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-smartwatches-under-5000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 5,000, a smartwatch is really a fitness band with a bigger screen. It counts steps, tracks heart rate and sleep, and shows notifications, and many can take calls over Bluetooth.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-5-active\">Redmi Watch 5 Active</a>: Rs 4,499. The most reliable choice here, lasting up to about 18 days per charge.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/boat-wave-call-3\">boAt Wave Call 3</a>: Rs 3,199. Bluetooth calling and up to about 10 days of battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/ultima-watch-active\">Ultima Watch Active</a>: Rs 4,299. A local favourite that does the basics well.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Keep expectations realistic</h2>\n<p>None of these have built-in GPS, so runs and walks are estimated rather than mapped. Heart-rate and SpO2 readings are rough guides, not medical measurements. If accurate tracking matters, stretch to a watch with GPS in our <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-20000-nepal\">under Rs 20,000</a> guide.</p>','gadgets/2026/redmi-watch-5-active.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(105,20,'Best Smartwatches Under Rs 10,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-smartwatches-under-10000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Between Rs 5,000 and Rs 10,000, smartwatches get AMOLED screens that are easy to read in sunlight, and much better battery life.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/honor-watch-x5i\">Honor Watch X5i</a>: Rs 8,999. An AMOLED screen and up to about three weeks of typical use. Our top pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/mwc-aether-one-watch-pro\">MWC Aether One Watch Pro</a>: Rs 6,999. A rare find at this price: AMOLED <em>and</em> built-in GPS.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/galaxy-fit-3\">Samsung Galaxy Fit 3</a>: Rs 7,999. A slim band with a big AMOLED screen, and the obvious choice for Samsung phone owners.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/huawei-band-10\">Huawei Band 10</a>: Rs 7,990. Light, accurate and long-lasting.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>boAt\'s <a href=\"/products/boat-ultima-regal\">Ultima Regal</a> (Rs 6,099) looks more like a classic watch, but its tracking is less accurate. For GPS and better health tracking, see <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-20000-nepal\">under Rs 20,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/honor-watch-x5i.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(106,20,'Best Smartwatches Under Rs 20,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-smartwatches-under-20000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Rs 10,000–20,000 is the best value range for smartwatches in Nepal. Most watches here have AMOLED screens, built-in GPS and battery life measured in weeks.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-active\">Redmi Watch 6 Active</a>: Rs 10,999. AMOLED, GPS and up to about 12 days of normal use. The value pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-watch-6-lite\">Redmi Watch 6 Lite</a>: Rs 14,999. A step up in design, with the same strong battery life.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/cmf-watch-3-pro\">CMF Watch 3 Pro</a>: Rs 12,999. A stylish round design with accurate GPS.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/realme-watch-s5\">Realme Watch S5</a>: Rs 15,999. A good screen and GPS, with up to 16 days of battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/amazfit-gtr-mini\">Amazfit GTR Mini</a>: Rs 17,499. A compact, classic-looking watch for smaller wrists.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All of these work with Android and iPhone. Built-in GPS means you can leave your phone at home on a morning walk and still get an accurate route. For more premium watches, see <a href=\"/guides/best-smartwatches-under-30000-nepal\">under Rs 30,000</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/redmi-watch-6-lite.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(107,20,'Best Tablets Under Rs 30,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-tablets-under-30000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Under Rs 30,000 is the right budget for a tablet that\'s mainly for YouTube, Netflix, reading and online classes. Big batteries are common at this price, but fast chips aren\'t.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2\">Redmi Pad 2 (11-inch)</a>: Rs 29,999. A sharp 2.5K screen, quad speakers and a 9,000mAh battery. Our top pick.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/honor-pad-x8b\">Honor Pad X8b</a>: Rs 29,999. A huge 10,100mAh battery.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2-9-7\">Redmi Pad 2 9.7</a>: Rs 25,999. Smaller and lighter, a good size for children.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-a11\">Samsung Galaxy Tab A11</a>: Rs 21,999. The cheapest Samsung, with long software support.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Blackview and Infinix sell many tablets at this price, such as the <a href=\"/products/infinix-xpad-20-pro\">Infinix XPAD 20 Pro</a>. They\'re fine for videos, but screens and software support are usually weaker than Xiaomi\'s or Samsung\'s. For note-taking with a pen, see our <a href=\"/guides/best-tablets-nepal\">tablet guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/infinix-xpad-20-pro.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00'),(108,20,'Best Tablets Under Rs 50,000 in Nepal (November 2026)','best-tablets-under-50000-nepal','buying-guide','<p>Between Rs 30,000 and Rs 50,000, tablets get faster chips and sharper, smoother screens. This is good territory for students who take notes and for light creative work.</p>\n<h2>Our picks</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"/products/xiaomi-pad-7\">Xiaomi Pad 7</a>: Rs 44,999. A 3.2K 144Hz screen and a Snapdragon 7+ Gen 3. The best performance in this range.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-pad-go-2\">OnePlus Pad Go 2</a>: Rs 49,999. A 10,050mAh battery and a Dimensity 7300, with smooth software.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/oneplus-pad-lite\">OnePlus Pad Lite</a>: Rs 34,999. A cheaper OnePlus with a big battery, and there\'s an LTE version for using data away from Wi-Fi.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/products/redmi-pad-2\">Redmi Pad 2 (11-inch)</a>: from Rs 29,999. If you\'d rather save, it\'s still excellent for watching and reading.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you want to write by hand, check whether a pen is supported and if it\'s included. The <a href=\"/products/samsung-galaxy-tab-s10-fe\">Galaxy Tab S10 FE</a> (Rs 74,999) is above this budget but comes with an S Pen. More options are in our <a href=\"/guides/best-tablets-nepal\">tablet guide</a>.</p>','gadgets/2026/xiaomi-pad-7.webp',1,'2026-11-22 18:15:00','2026-11-22 18:15:00');
